            <ArticleTitle>Severe stenosis of the left main coronary artery with endarterectomy and graft: 33-year follow-up.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1559-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In 1964, a patient with symptomatic, severe left main coronary artery stenosis underwent operative treatment. Endarterectomy and pericardial patch grafting were performed successfully. The original operation is described, and the 33-year follow-up is provided.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
